[00:00.00]The diagram above clearly illustrates that dramatic elevation has occurred in the recruitment of Master of Professional Accounting (MPAcc) from 2010 to 2016.
[00:13.93]In 2010,
[00:14.65]the number was at a low level,
[00:17.13]only about 10,000.
[00:18.78]Surprisingly,
[00:20.12]within no more than seven years it reached to 40,000 in 2016.
[00:25.28]Some driving factors that contribute to the above-mentioned changes may be summarized as follows.
[00:33.95]First and foremost,
[00:35.71]China has become particularly active in the economy,
[00:40.35]which leads to the increasing demand for qualified accountants.
[00:46.03]In addition,
[00:47.16]the development of the job market on the whole cannot keep pace with the expansion of college graduates,
[00:56.14]which obliges a large number of students to stay on campus for another two or three years to get better prepared for their career.
[01:07.18]Taking all these factors into account,
[01:10.59]we may predict that with the speedy development of our society,
[01:16.06]the number of recruitment of MPAcc will keep growing in the forthcoming decade.
